// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\ai-chat-webui\\supabase\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":78,"lines":["+# Self-hosted Supabase backend","+","+This folder contains everything needed to run the app's own Supabase stack:","+Postgres (with the workspace schema in `migrations/`), Supabase Auth (GoTrue),","+PostgREST, and a small Caddy gateway that exposes them as one Supabase URL.","+","+The managed Supabase cloud, Clerk, WorkOS, and hand-rolled password storage","+are intentionally not used here: auth data stays on infrastructure you operate.","+","+## 1. Configure secrets","+","+```bash","+cp supabase/.env.example supabase/.env","+```","+","+Then replace every `change-me-...` value. Generate strong values with:","+","+```bash","+openssl rand -hex 32","+openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -d '\\n'","+```","+","+Never commit `supabase/.env`. The root `.gitignore` already excludes `.env`","+files everywhere. The browser only ever receives the public gateway URL and","+the anon key; row-level security is what protects user data.","+","+## 2. Start the stack","+","+```bash","+docker compose --env-file supabase/.env -f supabase/docker-compose.yml up -d db auth rest gateway","+```","+","+Apply the workspace schema once per database:","+","+```bash","+docker compose --env-file supabase/.env -f supabase/docker-compose.yml exec db \\","+  psql -U postgres -d postgres -f /migrations/0001_workspace.sql","+```","+","+Later schema changes must be added as new immutable files","+(`0002_*.sql`, `0003_*.sql`, ...) and applied explicitly with `psql`.","+","+## 3. Check the services","+","+- Gateway health: `SUPABASE_PUBLIC_URL/health`","+- Auth health: `http://127.0.0.1:9999/health` (default local port)","+- PostgREST is reachable only through `/rest/v1/...` on the gateway.","+","+If SMTP variables are empty, set `GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true` for local","+development only. Without working SMTP and without autoconfirm, new accounts","+cannot confirm their email address.","+","+## 4. Back up and restore","+","+Back up (run on a schedule in production):","+","+```bash","+docker compose --env-file supabase/.env -f supabase/docker-compose.yml exec db \\","+  pg_dump -U postgres -d postgres -Fc > \"backup-$(date +%F).dump\"","+```","+","+Restore into a fresh stack:","+","+```bash","+docker compose --env-file supabase/.env -f supabase/docker-compose.yml up -d db","+docker compose --env-file supabase/.env -f supabase/docker-compose.yml exec -T db \\","+  pg_restore -U postgres -d postgres --clean < backup-YYYY-MM-DD.dump","+docker compose --env-file supabase/.env -f supabase/docker-compose.yml up -d auth rest gateway","+```","+","+## 5. Production notes","+","+- Keep all component ports bound to localhost and terminate TLS in a reverse","+  proxy. Expose only the app and the gateway's public URL.","+- Record the deployed image digests after the first successful deploy and pin","+  them in `supabase/.env` via the `*_IMAGE` variables.","+- You are responsible for OS patching, Postgres maintenance, backups,","+  monitoring, and stack updates."]}]}]}
